course: dictionary
lesson: 9372
title: A spoonful of meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A spoonful is the amount a spoon can hold. The word is made of spoon and ful, and -ful means "as much as fits in". So a spoonful of sugar is exactly as much sugar as one spoon holds.
explain: Cooks and scientists use spoonfuls to measure. A teaspoon is small and a tablespoon is bigger, so a recipe may ask for one spoonful of cinnamon. The clue words help: «a level spoonful» is filled to the top and no more, while «a heaped spoonful» is piled above the rim.
explain: Medicine is often measured in spoonfuls too, but only an adult should give it, and the right amount matters. «Swallowing a spoonful of a dry powder like cinnamon for a dare can make you choke and hurt your lungs.» That is a warning, not a game: never try it.
explain: Look at the clues in «Live yoghurt contains living bacteria that are harmless or helpful; a spoonful in warm milk can make more yoghurt.» The words "in warm milk" show that a spoonful is a small measured amount of yoghurt, added to something else.
fact: A spoonful is the amount a spoon holds.
fact: The plural of spoonful is spoonfuls, as in «two spoonfuls of sugar».
fact: «A spoonful of» is a useful phrase, as in «a spoonful of honey».
fact: Cooks and scientists use spoonfuls to measure, and a teaspoon is smaller than a tablespoon.
fact: Never swallow a spoonful of anything as a dare, and ask an adult to measure medicine.
exercise: What is a spoonful? | A big bowl for soup | The name of a kitchen | A spoon that is broken | *The amount a spoon holds
exercise: Which is the correct plural of spoonful? | spoonsful | *spoonfuls | spoonful's | spoonfulls
exercise: A recipe says «one level spoonful of salt». What does level mean here? | Piled high above the top | Salt that is wet | Spoon held sideways | *Filled exactly to the top, not heaped
test: Why should an adult check how much medicine goes in the spoonful? | Because spoons are sticky | *Because the right amount matters for health | Because it is a game | Because medicine tastes nice
test: The yoghurt sentence says «a spoonful in warm milk can make more yoghurt». What is a spoonful here? | A large bowl of milk | A cold drink | *A small measured amount | A type of yoghurt
exam: Which phrase means one spoon's worth of sugar? | *a spoonful of sugar | a spoonfuls of sugar | a spoons of sugar | two spoonful of sugar
